  ('ph-real-life-foundation', 'Scholar sponsors and donors', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'education', false, 'Monthly or one-off gift', '{}', 'Real LIFE invites one-time or monthly gifts (suggested PHP 1,000, 5,000 or 10,000) and full-year scholar sponsorships covering tuition, supplies and retreats for students from poor families.

Source: https://reallife.ph/get-involved/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-real-life-foundation', 'Corporate CSR partners', 'partners', 'ongoing', 0, 'education', false, 'Annual partnership', array['CSR']::text[], 'The foundation is seeking companies for annual CSR giving, employee matching and Benevity-linked giving to fund its scholars.

Source: https://reallife.ph/get-involved/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-action-international-ph', 'Vocational instructors for at-risk youth', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 3, 'work', false, '5 years', array['Auto body', 'Refrigeration', 'Cooking', 'Tailoring']::text[], 'Instructors are needed in auto body, refrigeration and metal shop (for young men) and food preparation, salon and sewing (for young women) to train youth from poor families. Five-year commitment, basic Tagalog, youth-discipleship experience, and willingness to train a Filipino successor.

Source: https://www.actioninternational.org/opportunities-detail/philippines-vocational-instructors', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-emmanuel-international-errp', 'Regional program officer for Mindanao', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'leadership', false, 'Long-term (support-raised)', array['Project management', 'Community development', 'Church planting']::text[], 'A program officer (single or couple) is sought for 2026 to lead all of the agency''s Mindanao projects: outreach to unreached groups, training local leaders, community development, relief coordination, and budgets and reporting. Cross-cultural experience and ability to raise support are expected.

Source: https://oscar.org.uk/assets/files/jobs/program-officer-in-mindanao-philippines/2026-Philippines-Ministry-opportunity-in-Mindanao-job-description.pdf', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-chosen-children-village', 'October 2026 wishlist: food, milk and pantry staples', 'supplies', 'soon', 0, 'food', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The village''s October 2026 wishlist asks for fresh meat, fish, fruit, vegetables and eggs. It also asks for milk (fresh, condensed and powder), PediaSure/Similac 1-3, breakfast items, sugar, canned goods, rice, monggo beans, flour and condiments to feed the resident children.

Source: https://chosenchildrenfoundation.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/October-2026-Village-Wishlist.png', '2026-10-01'),
  ('ph-chosen-children-village', 'Maintenance and office supplies for the village', 'supplies', 'soon', 0, 'shelter', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The October 2026 wishlist lists maintenance items: plastic rakes and broomsticks, dark green, white enamel and latex paint, roof paint, brushes and rollers, 1/4 plywood, a pressure washer and an electric leaf blower. For the admin office it asks for double-sided tape, A4 specialty paper and matte photo paper.

Source: https://chosenchildrenfoundation.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/October-2026-Village-Wishlist.png', '2026-10-01'),
  ('ph-chosen-children-village', 'Child sponsors for children with disabilities', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', true, 'monthly gift', '{}', 'The foundation says child sponsorship is what lets it house, educate, rehabilitate and train its residents with physical and intellectual disabilities. Sponsorship is also the first item on the October 2026 wishlist.

Source: https://chosenchildrenfoundation.com/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-chosen-children-village', 'Volunteers for daily childcare and community services', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', false, null, array['Childcare']::text[], 'The village wants volunteers to help with daily care of the children and with its community services, and takes sign-ups through an online form. Groups can also join a short immersion program to work, eat and play alongside the teens and young adults who live there.

Source: https://chosenchildrenfoundation.com/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-chosen-children-village', 'OJT placements for SPED, PT, OT and social work students', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 0, 'health', false, 'on-the-job training term', array['Special Education', 'Physical Therapy', 'Occupational Therapy', 'Social Work']::text[], 'Chosen Children Village offers on-the-job training to college students majoring in Special Education, Physical Therapy, Occupational Therapy, Social Work and Caregiving. Trainees support its therapeutic care for residents with disabilities.

Source: https://chosenchildrenfoundation.com/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-childrens-shelter-of-cebu', 'Medical fund for shelter children ($116,794)', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'health', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'A special project of $116,794 for the children''s doctor visits, hospital stays, therapies, medical supplies and immunizations. Between a quarter and half of the shelter''s children have special needs.

Source: https://cebushelter.org/donate/projects', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-childrens-shelter-of-cebu', 'Education fund and Cebu Children of Hope School days', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'education', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The Education project ($216,001) covers the operating budget of Cebu Children of Hope School plus high school and college tuition, books, supplies and uniforms. Donors can also sponsor a single school day for $475.

Source: https://cebushelter.org/donate/projects', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-childrens-shelter-of-cebu', 'Family Traditions fund: birthdays, Christmas and activities', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'A $56,517 special project that pays for birthday parties, Christmas gifts, events and activities, children''s allowances and appreciation for staff. These give the children a normal family life.

Source: https://cebushelter.org/donate/projects', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-childrens-shelter-of-cebu', 'Amazon wishlist for the Cebu children''s homes', 'supplies', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The shelter keeps a public Amazon wishlist (amazon.com/hz/wishlist/ls/7SNAMTOQQ7MK) of items for its homes. Supporters can buy and send these items directly.

Source: https://cebushelter.org/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-kids-international-ministries', '3-month immersion volunteers', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', false, '3 months on site', '{}', 'KIDS offers a 3-month immersion for volunteers who want more than a two- or three-week trip. Volunteers serve its children''s homes, school, feeding and youth programs in Cuatro. Lodging for stays of 1 to 3 months costs about $40 per person per night.

Source: https://www.kidsim.org/volunteer', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-kids-international-ministries', 'One-year interns with training and discipleship', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'discipleship', false, '1 year', '{}', 'A one-year internship for people who want a longer-term experience, with training and discipleship, serving in KIDS ministries such as Church Connect. KIDS also recruits full-time missionaries.

Source: https://www.kidsim.org/volunteer', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-kids-international-ministries', 'Construction mission teams for classrooms and repairs', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'shelter', false, 'short-term trip, dates arranged case by case', array['Construction']::text[], 'KIDS hosts construction teams to build classrooms, pour concrete floors, rebuild rooms and bathrooms, and handle smaller maintenance jobs at its base in Cuatro. It costs $60 per person per night for stays of 30 days or less, including lodging, meals and airport transfers. The base can host 60 to 100 people.

Source: https://www.kidsim.org/volunteer/construction-mission-trip', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-kids-international-ministries', 'Hope Alive Hospital (opening 2027) building fund', 'funding', 'soon', 0, 'health', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'KIDS is raising support for Hope Alive Hospital, a Christ-centered hospital planned to open in 2027. It will grow out of the ministry''s free Hope Alive pregnancy and birthing clinic for poor mothers.

Source: https://www.kidsim.org/donate', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-kids-international-ministries', 'Meals and Values feeding program support', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'food', true, 'monthly gift', '{}', 'Through partner local churches, the Meals and Values program serves children in poor communities a weekly meal of lugaw (rice porridge) and builds relationships with them. The ministry takes one-time and monthly gifts for it.

Source: https://www.kidsim.org/ministries/meals-and-values', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-action-international-ph', 'Street Children Worker (2+ years)', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 1, 'children', false, '2 years minimum', array['Social work', 'Counseling', 'Bible teaching']::text[], 'Brand New Day wants missionaries to reach street children and their families in Silang and Dasmarinas through street outreach, Bible studies, family counseling and a scholarship program. Workers may also start livelihood or shelter initiatives. Applicants need at least a year of Bible training and a pastoral recommendation.

Source: http://www.actioninternational.org/opportunities-detail/philippines-street-children-worker-brand-new-day', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-action-international-ph', 'Brand New Day missions intern', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', false, 'internship term', array['Teaching English', 'Music', 'Tagalog']::text[], 'Interns build relationships with street kids, youth and staff. They teach English or other skills such as music, visit families in slum communities, help cook and write newsletters, and pick up basic Tagalog along the way.

Source: http://www.actioninternational.org/opportunities-detail/philippines-brand-new-day-missions-intern', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-action-international-ph', 'Vocational instructors: auto body, refrigeration, metal shop', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 0, 'work', false, '5 years minimum', array['Auto body repair', 'Refrigeration', 'Metalwork', 'Tagalog']::text[], 'ACTION''s vocational school in Silang needs men skilled in auto body, refrigeration and metal shop to train young people from poor families in Metro Manila and nearby provinces. Instructors disciple students, manage the shops and train Filipino successors.

Source: http://www.actioninternational.org/opportunities-detail/philippines-vocational-instructors', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-action-international-ph', 'Vocational instructors: food prep, salon, seamstress', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 0, 'work', false, '5 years minimum', array['Food preparation', 'Cosmetology', 'Sewing', 'Tagalog']::text[], 'The same Silang vocational program needs women to teach food preparation, salon and sewing to young women from low-income families. Instructors bring Biblical teaching into the shop setting and work toward self-supporting shops run by national staff.

Source: http://www.actioninternational.org/opportunities-detail/philippines-vocational-instructors', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-action-international-ph', 'Working Hands discipleship internship for tradesmen', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'work', false, 'internship term', array['Trade skills']::text[], 'A men-only internship in which interns use their trade skills to help missionaries give young men vocational training and discipleship.

Source: https://www.actioninternational.org/opportunities/?loid=7874', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-tahanan-sta-luisa', 'Annual appeal for girl survivors of abuse ($112,784 to go)', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'trauma', true, 'one-off or monthly gift', '{}', 'The GlobalGiving appeal has raised about $137,000 of its $250,000 goal. Gift levels: $10 for school supplies, $90 for a yearly psychological assessment, $250 for counseling and art or play therapy, and $3,000 for school preparation and skills training for girls rescued from the streets.

Source: https://cl.globalgiving.org/projects/tahananannualappeal/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-tahanan-ng-pagmamahal', 'Volunteers for the children''s home in Pasig', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', false, null, array['Filipino or English', 'Childcare']::text[], 'The home takes volunteers aged 18 and over who speak Filipino or English and are self-reliant, flexible and adaptable. Applicants send a CV and application form by email and must show a medical clearance (chest x-ray and hepatitis profile).

Source: https://tahananngpagmamahal.org/get-involved/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-tahanan-ng-pagmamahal', 'In-kind: milk, rice, produce, condiments, garbage bags', 'supplies', 'ongoing', 0, 'food', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The home asks for milk products (Bear Brand, Bonnamil, Bonna Kid and Bonna Kid Pre-School), rice, fruits, vegetables, condiments such as soy sauce, cooking oil, salt, ketchup and sugar, and large black garbage bags.

Source: https://tahananngpagmamahal.org/get-involved/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-tahanan-ng-pagmamahal', 'Operating support: shelter costs, food, medical care and schooling', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', true, 'one-off or monthly gift', '{}', 'Cash gifts pay for staff training and transport, the shelter''s utilities, repairs and salaries, and each child''s food, medical care, psychosocial support and education. As of mid-2026 the home cared for about 41 children aged 6 months to 14 years.

Source: https://tahananngpagmamahal.org/get-involved/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-manaoag-christian-childrens-home', 'Volunteer teachers for the homeschool program', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'education', false, null, array['Teaching', 'Elementary education']::text[], 'The children''s home runs an elementary homeschool program taught by volunteer teachers. The foundation also invites people to spend a working vacation serving at its orphanages.

Source: https://www.filipino-orphans.org/manaoag-christian-childrens-home/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-manaoag-christian-childrens-home', 'Volunteer nurses for regular health checks', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 0, 'health', false, 'recurring visits', array['Nursing', 'Pediatrics']::text[], 'The home relies on volunteer nurses to give its infants and young children regular health checks.

Source: https://www.filipino-orphans.org/manaoag-christian-childrens-home/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-manaoag-christian-childrens-home', 'Clothing, shoes, school supplies and toys', 'supplies', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The Philippines Orphanage Foundation lists clothing, shoes, school supplies and toys as current needs for its orphanages, and the home also takes food and other basic goods.

Source: https://www.filipino-orphans.org/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-hospicio-de-san-jose', 'Milk formula, canned goods and pantry items for residents', 'supplies', 'ongoing', 0, 'food', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Hospicio''s wishlist asks for milk formula (NAN HW Two, Bear Brand, Nestogen, Nido, Ensure Gold, PediaSure 3+), canned meat, tuna and sardines, noodles and pasta, oats, bread, cooking oil, sugar, condiments and fresh milk drinks. These feed its children, elderly and residents in crisis.

Source: https://hospiciodesanjose.org/support/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-hospicio-de-san-jose', 'Diapers, toiletries and cleaning supplies', 'supplies', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The list includes baby diapers (XL, XXL), adult diapers, baby wipes, lotions, soap, shampoo and toothpaste. It also asks for laundry detergent, bleach, dishwashing liquid, toilet cleaner, garbage bags and rubber gloves, plus school and office supplies such as bond paper, pads, tape and calculators.

Source: https://hospiciodesanjose.org/support/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-hospicio-de-san-jose', 'Appliances: water pressure tank, laptop, printer, refrigerator', 'supplies', 'soon', 0, 'shelter', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Equipment requests include a pressure tank for the Tahan crisis center''s water tank (about PHP 13,000), a laptop and a printer-scanner for admin and trainings, a refrigerator, a bathroom water heater, wall fans, a 2.5HP split-type aircon, a DSLR camera and a campus-wide audio system.

Source: https://hospiciodesanjose.org/support/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-hospicio-de-san-jose', 'Construction supplies for roofing, ceilings and gutters', 'supplies', 'soon', 0, 'shelter', false, 'one-off gift', array['Construction']::text[], 'Hospicio asks donors to call and discuss gifts of construction materials for repairs to roofing, ceilings and gutters on its historic campus.

Source: https://hospiciodesanjose.org/support/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-hospicio-de-san-jose', 'Volunteers to share time and talents', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', false, null, '{}', 'Hospicio welcomes volunteers to serve its children, elderly, residents with special needs and people in crisis, and asks them to inquire through its contact form.

Source: https://hospiciodesanjose.org/support/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-preda-foundation', 'Interns in psychology, social work and human rights law', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 0, 'trauma', false, 'internship term', array['Psychology', 'Social work', 'Human rights law', 'Counseling']::text[], 'Preda takes Filipino and international students in psychology, social work, human rights law, counseling and the humanities. Senior social workers and therapists supervise them as they join daily life in the children''s homes, home visits, jail visits and legal case work.

Source: https://www.preda.org/internship/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-preda-foundation', 'Fund a rescue or a year of care for an abused child', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', true, 'one-off or yearly gift', '{}', 'EUR 150 funds the rescue of a child from abusers, and EUR 75 covers legal work to move a child from jail to the boys'' home. EUR 1,500 to 2,500 a year covers shelter, therapy, schooling, food and personal items for a rescued child.

Source: https://www.preda.org/donate/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-mary-queen-of-heaven-missionaries', 'Expand the Home of Love for trafficking survivors', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'trauma', true, 'monthly gift', '{}', 'The sisters are raising funds to expand the Home of Love in Tuburan so it can take in more girls and women rescued from sex trafficking. $100 a month cares for one girl in the home.

Source: https://www.mqhm.org/donate', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-mary-queen-of-heaven-missionaries', 'Regina Coeli school sponsorships for rural children', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'education', true, 'monthly gift', '{}', 'The Regina Coeli Educational Program keeps rural children in school as a defense against exploitation. It aims to grow from about 18,000 to 35,000 students a year but has stalled for lack of funds. $25 a month enrolls one child with supplies, bag and fees.

Source: https://www.mqhm.org/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-wipe-every-tear', 'Fund daily meal outreach to women in the bars', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'food', true, 'one-off or monthly gift', '{}', 'The Hope Revive giving tier pays for meal outreach run with Church So Blessed in Angeles City, which serves 200+ meals a day to women working in bars at under $2 per meal. The meals open the door to relationships and offers of escape.

Source: https://www.wipeeverytear.org/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-wipe-every-tear', 'Sponsor safe homes and survivors'' college education', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'trauma', true, 'monthly gift', '{}', 'The House Revive and Heart Revive tiers fund safe homes for women and children leaving sex trafficking, and the women''s education program, which pays for survivors'' college studies.

Source: https://www.wipeeverytear.org/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-wipe-every-tear', 'Volunteers for meal outreach in Angeles City', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'trauma', false, null, '{}', 'Volunteers can join the daily meal outreach with Church So Blessed in Angeles City, serving meals to women in the bars. Vision trips are paused for now.

Source: https://www.wipeeverytear.org/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-noahs-ark-ministries-banaue', 'Support health, nutrition, education and respite care in Ifugao', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', true, 'one-off or monthly gift', '{}', 'Gifts pay for healthcare, nutrition, schooling and respite care for the home''s orphaned, abandoned and malnourished children. They also fund its special needs learning centre and elementary and high school scholarships for mountain families in Banaue.

Source: https://paoc.org/donate/LindaVeldhuizen', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-obeds-house-ministries', 'Support 24/7 residential care for neglected children', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Obed''s House cares around the clock for 13 neglected children aged 5 to 12 in General Santos City. Suggested gifts of $30, $50 or $100 go to its ongoing residential care.

Source: https://give.abwe.org/projects/obed-s-house-ministries', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-little-children-of-the-philippines', 'Urgent 2026 appeal: $200,000 to meet the year''s budget', 'funding', 'urgent', 0, 'children', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The ministry says it needs $200,000 to finish 2026 with all program budgets met, and matching donors will double the first $40,000. The budgets cover its health, education, livelihood and faith programs for children at risk in Dumaguete.

Source: https://littlechildren.org/urgent-needs-2026/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-little-children-of-the-philippines', 'International volunteers in Dumaguete', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', false, null, '{}', 'Little Children of the Philippines invites volunteers to Dumaguete City to help rescue children from poverty, neglect and abuse. Volunteers can bring their training to strengthen existing programs or start new ones.

Source: https://littlechildren.org/get-involved/volunteer/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-little-children-of-the-philippines', 'Angel Christmas Cards fundraiser (order by Dec 5)', 'funding', 'soon', 0, 'fundraising', true, 'one-off purchase', '{}', 'The ministry sells cards drawn by Filipino students in its Christmas card contest for $2 each, with a minimum of 5. Proceeds fund its programs, and orders are due by December 5.

Source: https://littlechildren.org/angel-christmas-cards/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-island-kids-philippines', 'On-site volunteers for the community learning center', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', false, null, array['Childcare', 'Creativity']::text[], 'Island Kids is looking for motivated, proactive and creative volunteers with a heart for children to join daily life at its Cagayan de Oro learning center. Applicants request an information sheet and application form from volunteer@islandkids.ch.

Source: https://islandkids.ch/volunteers/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-island-kids-philippines', 'Child sponsorships and scholarships through university', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'education', true, 'monthly gift', '{}', 'The charity seeks child sponsors and donations for its village school, scholarships up to university level and its regenerative farm. These serve children and families from Cagayan de Oro''s waste-picker community.

Source: https://www.islandkids.ch/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-shepherd-of-the-hills-baguio', 'Sponsor a child''s schooling ($35/month)', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'education', true, 'monthly gift', '{}', '$35 a month covers a child''s school costs, uniform, shoes, backpack, lunches and books, and yearly sponsors can write to their child. Partner Airline Ambassadors also runs April and October trips to visit the home, and a college sponsorship program has started.

Source: https://airlineamb.org/philippines-sponsorship-program/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-philippine-childrens-mission', 'Volunteers for children''s home and education programs', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', false, null, '{}', 'The Balagtas home invites volunteers through its inquiry form. Volunteers help with its care of orphans and children of parents with leprosy or other debilitating illnesses, its schooling and life-skills programs, and community outings and spiritual activities.

Source: https://pcmhome.org/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-silliman-university', 'Full-time Software Developer, ICT Division', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'technology', false, 'Full-time staff position', array['Software development', 'IT/Computer Science', 'Technical documentation']::text[], 'Silliman''s ICT Division wants a developer to build and maintain software for university departments, and to test, debug and document it. The role is open to IT or Computer Science graduates, including fresh graduates. Applicants send a letter of intent and CV with the subject ''ICT Software Developer''.

Source: https://su.edu.ph/su-ict-division-is-hiring-a-full-time-software-developer/', '2026-08-18'),
  ('ph-silliman-university', 'Full-time Social Work Instructor', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'education', false, 'Full-time faculty', array['MS Social Work', 'Registered Social Worker', 'Teaching']::text[], 'The Social Work Department is hiring a full-time instructor. Candidates need a master''s in social work, a valid PRC license and membership in the PASW and NASWE professional bodies. A doctorate is preferred.

Source: https://su.edu.ph/su-social-work-department-is-hiring-a-full-time-instructor/', '2026-06-01'),
  ('ph-silliman-university', 'Elementary Filipino III Teacher', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'education', false, 'Full-time teacher', array['LPT license', 'Filipino language', 'Literacy']::text[], 'The School of Basic Education''s elementary school needs a full-time Filipino teacher for Grade 3. Applicants should be licensed professional teachers with a master''s degree or units toward one. A background in reading intervention or literacy development is preferred.

Source: https://su.edu.ph/school-of-basic-education-sbe-elementary-school-is-hiring-a-full-time-instructor-for-filipino-iii/', '2026-06-23'),
  ('ph-silliman-university', 'Elementary English III Teacher', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'education', false, 'Full-time teacher', array['LPT license', 'English/Reading', 'Literacy']::text[], 'The School of Basic Education''s elementary school is hiring a full-time Grade 3 English teacher. The role calls for a licensed professional teacher with a master''s degree or units toward one. Experience in elementary reading and language instruction is preferred.

Source: https://su.edu.ph/school-of-basic-education-sbe-elementary-school-is-hiring-a-full-time-instructor-for-english-iii/', '2026-06-23'),
  ('ph-silliman-university', 'University Associate Counsel', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'legal', false, 'Full-time staff position', array['Philippine Bar', 'Contract review', 'Labor relations']::text[], 'Silliman''s Legal and Compliance Division wants a lawyer with 1-3 years of practice. The lawyer would review contracts, prepare pleadings, notarize documents and represent the administration in labor and disciplinary matters. Bar membership and MCLE compliance are required.

Source: https://su.edu.ph/the-silliman-university-legal-and-compliance-division-is-hiring-a-full-time-university-associate-counsel/', '2026-08-18'),
  ('ph-silliman-university', 'Laboratory Farm Supervisor, College of Agriculture', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'work', false, 'Full-time staff position', array['Agriculture degree', 'Farm operations', 'Staff supervision']::text[], 'The College of Agriculture needs a supervisor to run its teaching farm day to day. The role covers crop and livestock work, equipment, biosecurity and safety, farm staff and students'' hands-on learning. An agriculture degree is required and a PRC agriculturist license is preferred.

Source: https://su.edu.ph/laboratory-farm-supervisor/', '2026-09-17'),
  ('ph-silliman-university', 'Director, Dr. Mariano C. Lao Global Studies Center', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'leadership', false, 'Full-time leadership role', array['Program development', 'Partnerships', 'Online/hybrid learning']::text[], 'Silliman is looking for a director to set strategy for its Global Studies Center. The director would build programs and university partnerships and manage the center''s marketing, operations and finances. A relevant master''s degree and experience designing educational programs are required.

Source: https://su.edu.ph/the-dr-mariano-c-lao-global-studies-center-is-searching-for-its-new-director/', '2026-09-16'),
  ('ph-silliman-university', 'Office Assistant, College of Engineering and Design', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'admin', false, 'Full-time staff position', array['Office administration']::text[], 'The College of Engineering and Design is hiring a full-time office assistant to support the college''s administration. Applications go to Silliman''s OD & HRM office as listed on the university careers page.

Source: https://su.edu.ph/college-of-engineering-and-design-is-hiring-a-full-time-office-assistant/', '2026-07-31'),
  ('ph-central-philippine-university', 'Full-time and part-time Social Work faculty', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 2, 'education', false, 'Full-time or part-time faculty', array['Social Work', 'Teaching']::text[], 'CPU''s jobs page lists full-time and part-time faculty openings in its Social Work Department. Inquiries go through the university''s information center.

Source: https://cpu.edu.ph/jobs/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-central-philippine-university', 'Network Systems Supervisor', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 1, 'technology', false, 'Full-time staff position', array['Networking', 'Systems administration']::text[], 'CPU is hiring a supervisor for its network systems, as listed on the university''s current jobs page.

Source: https://cpu.edu.ph/jobs/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-central-philippine-university', 'Build the new College of Law and Medicine complex', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'education', false, 'one-off gift or monthly pledge', '{}', 'CPU''s ''Together We Build'' campaign aims to raise PHP 250 million from 2025 to 2028 for a multi-storey building for its law and medicine colleges. The building will hold lecture halls, simulation rooms, a moot court and labs. Donors can adopt bricks from PHP 1,000 to PHP 50,000, give once, pledge monthly or partner as a company.

Source: https://cpu.edu.ph/resource-generation-campaign/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-faith-international-academy', 'School Principal', 'expertise', 'urgent', 1, 'leadership', false, '1 year+', array['School leadership', 'Staff development', 'Christian education']::text[], 'FIA lists a principal as a critical need: an experienced, creative leader to oversee daily operations, staff development and educational outcomes. Strong organizational and communication skills are required.

Source: https://www.fia.edu.ph/opportunities-list', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-faith-international-academy', 'Secondary Science Teachers (grades 6-12)', 'expertise', 'urgent', 2, 'education', false, '1 year+', array['Science teaching', 'Biology/Physics/Chemistry', 'AP courses']::text[], 'FIA needs at least two science teachers. In high school they would teach physical science, biology, earth and space, health, physics, chemistry and AP courses. In middle school they would teach life, physical and earth science. One to two years of teaching experience is preferred.

Source: https://www.fia.edu.ph/opportunities-list', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-faith-international-academy', 'Secondary Math Teachers (grades 6-12)', 'expertise', 'urgent', 2, 'education', false, '1 year+', array['Math teaching', 'AP Calculus']::text[], 'FIA lists at least two math positions as critical needs. The teachers would cover middle school general math and pre-algebra up through high school and AP courses. One to two years of teaching experience is preferred.

Source: https://www.fia.edu.ph/opportunities-list', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-faith-international-academy', 'Secondary Social Studies Teacher', 'expertise', 'urgent', 1, 'education', false, '1 year+', array['Social studies', 'History teaching']::text[], 'FIA needs a teacher for middle school world studies and history, with possible high school electives or AP courses. One to two years of teaching experience is preferred.

Source: https://www.fia.edu.ph/opportunities-list', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-obeds-house-ministries', 'English / homeschool teachers for children''s home', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 1, 'education', false, 'short-term to long-term tracks', array['Teaching English', 'Homeschooling', 'Patience with kids']::text[], 'Obed''s House wants a patient, organized teacher for its children aged 5-12. Many of them never attended school before arriving and struggle with literacy and math. The teacher would give Christian-based English or homeschool instruction. Short-, mid- and long-term and intern tracks are offered through ABWE.

Source: https://abwe.org/serve/opportunities/teachers-3/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-doane-rest', 'Guesthouse Assistant Manager', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 1, 'admin', false, 'short-term to long-term tracks', array['Hospitality', 'QuickBooks', 'Staff supervision']::text[], 'Doane Rest needs an assistant manager to coordinate daily hospitality. The role also covers budgets in QuickBooks and Microsoft 365, supervising staff and handling guest communications and reports. A heart for serving missionaries and pastors matters more than formal qualifications.

Source: https://abwe.org/serve/opportunities/doane-rest-assistant-manager/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-asian-theological-seminary', 'Seminary teacher (theology, mentoring, pastor training)', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 1, 'leadership', false, 'career mission placement', array['Master''s in theology', 'Teaching', 'Pastoral experience']::text[], 'WorldVenture is recruiting seminary teachers for institutions including Asian Theological Seminary in Manila, with further work in Bacolod and Davao. They would teach theology, mentor students and train about 40 pastors through a Pastoral Advancement Program. A master''s degree and experience as a pastor, professor or church planter are required.

Source: https://worldventure.com/popportunities/seminary-teacher/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-asian-theological-seminary', 'Student scholarships and faculty support', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'leadership', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'ATS asks for gifts toward faculty salaries, scholarships, operating costs and faculty development. Its WorldVenture partner page puts a student''s school expenses at about USD 1,000 a year. Donations can be made by bank deposit, check or the online portal, including GCash.

Source: https://worldventure.com/pministry/asian-theological-seminary-ats/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-biblical-seminary-of-the-philippines', 'Theological educator (BSOP, ATS, AGST or KTS)', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 1, 'leadership', false, '1 to 3 years, or 3 years+', array['Master''s+ in theology', 'Teaching', 'Filipino (willing to learn)']::text[], 'OMF is placing theological educators to teach theology, ministry and leadership and mentor future pastors. Placements are at the Biblical Seminary of the Philippines, Asian Theological Seminary, Asian Graduate School of Theology or Koinonia Theological Seminary in Davao. The role needs an advanced theology degree, ministry experience, fluent English and willingness to learn Filipino.

Source: https://opportunities.omf.org/mission-asia/detail/Theological-Educator/50419910', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-asia-pacific-theological-seminary', 'Scholarships, technology and facilities for APTS', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'leadership', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'APTS asks for gifts in four areas: infrastructure, equipment, technology and development. The money goes to scholarships, stronger academic programs, learning resources and campus upkeep for students training as pastors, missionaries and educators across Asia-Pacific.

Source: https://apts.edu/donate', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-bicol-center-christian-leadership', 'Professor to teach Bible subjects', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 1, 'leadership', false, null, array['Bible teaching', 'Mentoring']::text[], 'World Team lists a professor opening at the Bicol Bible College of Leadership. The professor would teach a range of Bible subjects to a small cohort of 15-18 students and mentor them so they can train others.

Source: https://ca.worldteam.org/opportunities/professor-philippines-2/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-bicol-center-christian-leadership', 'Support BCCL''s leader training in Bicol', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'leadership', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'North American Baptists'' 25th-anniversary article on BCCL invites gifts to the center and its leaders. BCCL is financially supported by NAB churches and runs entirely under Filipino leadership. It trains ministry leaders and runs food and Bible distribution.

Source: https://nabconference.org/2026/06/25-years-of-bccl-part-2/', '2026-06-01'),
  ('ph-imb-tribal-bible-college-bicol', 'Land and buildings for a tribal Bible college', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'leadership', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The project seeks USD 250,000 (about USD 97,800 raised so far) to start a self-supporting Bible college for tribal believers in Bicol. The money would buy land (USD 75,000), build classrooms, dorms, teacher housing and a USD 25,000 kitchen and dining hall, develop curriculum and supply rice until the first harvest.

Source: https://www.imb.org/give/project/tribal-bible-college/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-world-team-philippines', 'Livelihood entrepreneur for urban poor families', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 1, 'work', false, null, array['Entrepreneurship', 'Small business training', 'Creativity']::text[], 'World Team wants someone with entrepreneurial skills to help squatter families build income-generating projects and teach them to provide for their own families. The person would work alongside its church-planting teams.

Source: https://ca.worldteam.org/opportunities/livelihood-entrepreneur-philippines-2/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-world-team-philippines', 'Teach at Bible colleges and seminaries in Manila', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 1, 'leadership', false, null, array['Theological education', 'Teaching', 'Mentoring']::text[], 'World Team is recruiting teachers with Bible college or seminary experience to give theological education to national pastors and lay leaders at several Manila schools, and to mentor students.

Source: https://ca.worldteam.org/opportunities/teach-bible-school-or-seminary-students-philippines-2/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-world-team-philippines', 'Christian counselor for trauma-affected children', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 1, 'trauma', false, null, array['Christian counseling', 'Trauma care']::text[], 'World Team''s Justice and Mercy team is seeking a trained, experienced Christian counselor to serve children and others who have been through trauma.

Source: https://ca.worldteam.org/opportunities/counselor-philippines-2/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-world-team-naga', 'College ministry worker at five Naga universities', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 1, 'discipleship', false, null, array['Campus ministry', 'Evangelism', 'Mentoring']::text[], 'World Team is looking for workers to build relationships with college students and student volunteers at five universities in Naga City and in Caramoan. Together the universities enroll more than 50,000 students.

Source: https://ca.worldteam.org/opportunities/college-ministry-philippines-2/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-kmbi', 'Program Officer (vocational / livelihood fieldwork)', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'work', false, 'Full-time staff position', array['Vocational training', 'Fieldwork']::text[], 'KMBI''s careers page, current as of July 2026, lists a Program Officer for field-based work. Applicants should be vocational or K-12 qualified, and fresh graduates are welcome. Applications go through the QR code on the careers page.

Source: https://www.kmbi.org.ph/who-we-are/careers', '2026-07-02'),
  ('ph-kmbi', 'IT Technical Services Manager', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'technology', false, 'Full-time staff position', array['Backend development', 'AWS', 'IT management']::text[], 'KMBI needs an IT Technical Services Manager with a CS or IT degree, at least 5 years of backend development and AWS expertise. KMBI also lists a Senior Application Development Manager role.

Source: https://www.kmbi.org.ph/who-we-are/careers', '2026-07-02'),
  ('ph-kmbi', 'Audio Visual Production Officer (producer/writer)', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'media', false, 'Full-time staff position', array['Video production', 'Scriptwriting']::text[], 'KMBI is hiring a producer and writer to create audio-visual content for its microfinance and community-transformation work.

Source: https://www.kmbi.org.ph/who-we-are/careers', '2026-07-02'),
  ('ph-kmbi', 'Junior Internal Auditors (branch and head office)', 'expertise', 'soon', 3, 'admin', false, 'Full-time staff position', array['Auditing', 'Accounting']::text[], 'KMBI lists two branch-based junior internal auditor posts and one at its head office to audit its microfinance operations.

Source: https://www.kmbi.org.ph/who-we-are/careers', '2026-07-02'),
  ('ph-kmbi', 'Employee Welfare Associate', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'admin', false, 'Full-time staff position', array['Psychology/HR', 'Employee programs']::text[], 'KMBI is looking for a staff member with a psychology or HR background and at least a year running employee programs, to look after the welfare of its 1,200 staff.

Source: https://www.kmbi.org.ph/who-we-are/careers', '2026-07-02'),
  ('ph-international-care-ministries', 'Philippine Director of Health Operations', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 1, 'health', false, 'Full-time senior leadership', array['Public health', 'Program management', 'Partnerships']::text[], 'ICM is hiring a senior leader in Ortigas to manage and improve its health programs for ultra-poor families through strategic planning and partnership building.

Source: https://www.caremin.com/get-involved/careers', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-international-care-ministries', 'Junior Accountant', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 1, 'admin', false, 'Full-time staff position', array['Bookkeeping', 'Xero', 'Salesforce']::text[], 'ICM''s finance team needs a junior accountant in Ortigas. The work covers daily bookkeeping and month-end close in Xero, logging donations in Salesforce, issuing donor receipts and processing invoices and staff expenses.

Source: https://www.caremin.com/get-involved/careers', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-philippine-jesuit-prison-service', 'Sponsor schooling for children of inmates', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'education', false, 'ongoing sponsorship', '{}', 'PJPS asks for donors to sponsor the education of children of persons deprived of liberty. Its scholarship program supports students from grade school until they finish college.

Source: https://pjps.org.ph', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-philippine-jesuit-prison-service', 'Socio-pastoral care volunteers at New Bilibid Prison', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 10, 'prison', false, null, array['Counseling', 'Letter-writing', 'Medical missions']::text[], 'PJPS welcomes volunteers for its socio-pastoral care of vulnerable inmates: letter-writing, support, counseling, meals and medical missions. It also supports newly released people as they rejoin society.

Source: https://pjps.org.ph', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-ciw-prison-ministry', 'Stipends, food and Bible materials for women inmates', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'prison', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Gifts pay monthly stipends for the inmate leaders who run Bible studies, food and personal care items for prisoners, and discipleship materials at the Correctional Institution for Women. The ministry lost its founding missionary in 2022. A prison on Panay has asked for the same model. Suggested gifts are USD 30, 50 or 100.

Source: https://give.abwe.org/project/ciw-prison-ministry', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-brent-international-school', 'Swim Coach', 'expertise', 'soon', 1, 'education', false, 'Staff position', array['Swimming instruction', 'Water safety']::text[], 'Brent is hiring a swim coach at its Biñan, Laguna campus to teach swimming, keep students safe during pool activities and keep aquatics a supportive place to learn.

Source: https://ph.jobstreet.com/companies/brent-schools-inc-168559157635835', '2026-09-29'),
  ('ph-philippine-bible-society', 'Fund Bibles for isolated churches (Adopt-a-Church)', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'discipleship', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'PBS''s Adopt-a-Church and Funded Scripture Distribution programs give free Bibles and discipleship materials to isolated and disaster-hit churches that have none, along with leader training. Donations are taken through the PBS giving portal.

Source: https://bible.org.ph/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-philippine-bible-society', 'Support the Filipino Sign Language Bible translation', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'translation', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'PBS released 44 FSL video passages from Matthew, Mark and Luke in November 2025 and is working to complete the New Testament and then the full Bible in Filipino Sign Language. It invites gifts toward this demanding translation work.

Source: https://bible.org.ph/the-fsl-bible-a-translation-from-the-heart-for-the-filipino-deaf/', '2025-11-28'),
  ('ph-nazarene-mindoro-district', 'A Harvest of Hope in Mindoro – church multiplication ($6,000)', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'discipleship', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Project 154252 seeks $6,000 for seven young Nazarene congregations on Mindoro. Funds go to children''s programs, community evangelism, outreach to tribal and underserved people, and training local ministers.

Source: https://give.nazarene.org/donate/154252', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-nazarene-palawan', 'Pathways in Palawan – outreach, prison and tribal ministry ($6,000)', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'discipleship', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Project 154253 aims to raise $6,000 to equip local partners in Palawan for church outreach, neighborhood children''s programs, prison ministry and relationships with highland tribal communities.

Source: https://give.nazarene.org/donate/154253', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-nazarene-disaster-response-ph', 'Philippines Earthquake Response (Cebu and Mindanao)', 'funding', 'soon', 0, 'trauma', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'After the 2025 earthquakes in Cebu and Mindanao affected over 1.7 million people, Nazarene Disaster Response teams are giving food, water and medicine and running trauma-informed activities for children and teens. The fund is still accepting gifts.

Source: https://give.ncm.org/donate/140079', '2025-10-07'),
  ('ph-nazarene-disaster-response-ph', 'Philippines Disaster Response 2025 – equip churches to respond', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'refugees', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'This fund prepares local Nazarene churches and volunteers to respond quickly to typhoons, floods, fires and earthquakes with food, clean water, shelter and trauma care.

Source: https://give.ncm.org/donate/140130', '2025-11-01'),
  ('ph-giwo-philippines', 'Build a native church in Kabaya, Aklan ($2,245)', 'funding', 'soon', 0, 'worship', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'A new congregation in a previously unchurched barrio of Kabaya, Aklan has outgrown the home it meets in. The budget of $2,245 covers labor, materials, a restroom and a small kitchen, and members are supplying bamboo, site preparation and labor.

Source: https://www.giwo.org/current-projects/new-church-in-kabaya-manika-philippines', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-giwo-philippines', 'Buy land for Life Grace Church in Kalibo ($17,500)', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'worship', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Life Grace Church and Grace Bible Training Center have outgrown the carport they meet in next to the Shepherds Home. A half-acre lot nearby costs $17,500; the mission suggests 10 families giving $1,750 each.

Source: https://www.giwo.org/current-projects/life-grace-fellowship-in-madalag-aklan-philippines', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-giwo-philippines', 'Sound system for the Tapaz Bukidnon Tribal Center (~$4,400)', 'supplies', 'ongoing', 0, 'worship', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The Bukidnon tribal center in the Tapaz highlands is full every week with new believers. It needs 4 speakers ($928 each), 2 stands ($106 each) and 3 microphones ($155 each), about $4,389 in total, for the center and outreach events.

Source: https://www.giwo.org/current-projects/bukidnon-refuge-of-hope-center', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-giwo-philippines', 'Finish buying church land in Daja Sur ($2,450 remaining)', 'funding', 'soon', 0, 'worship', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Thirty-five families in Daja Sur meet in a member''s home and need a 550 sq m lot near the public square. Half of the $5,000 price has been raised, leaving $2,450.

Source: https://www.giwo.org/current-projects/new-church-plant-in-daja-sur-philippines', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-giwo-philippines', 'Renovate and enlarge Palayan, Mindoro church ($4,468)', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'worship', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The aging church building in Palayan, Mindoro has cracked walls and crumbling cement and is too small for the congregation. Phase 1 masonry costs $982 and Phase 2 ironwork, framing and painting costs $3,486. The church will pay for equipment rental.

Source: https://www.giwo.org/current-projects/palayan-house-of-worship-renovation', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-wesleyan-church-philippines-2', 'Rebuild six Wesleyan churches destroyed by the June 2026 quake', 'funding', 'urgent', 0, 'shelter', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The magnitude 7.8 earthquake on 8 June 2026 destroyed six Wesleyan churches, including Glan Wesleyan Church, and a district center in southern Mindanao. Gifts through the TWC-GP Emergency Relief Fund pay for aid to members, demolition and cleanup, rice and water, and long-term rebuilding. About $6,750 had been given by 18 June.

Source: https://www.wesleyan.org/philippines-earthquake-response-stand-with-our-wesleyan-family', '2026-06-18'),
  ('ph-camacop', 'Earthquake relief led by Alliance churches in South Cotabato', 'funding', 'urgent', 0, 'refugees', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Alliance churches in three districts are leading relief for families displaced by the June 2026 earthquake in South Cotabato and Sarangani. The Alliance Canada''s Global Emergency Response is raising funds for food, clean water, shelter and medical help.

Source: https://events.thealliancecanada.ca/updates/global-emergency-response-in-the-philippines', '2026-06-25'),
  ('ph-caritas-philippines', 'Sarangani earthquake relief and rehabilitation fund', 'funding', 'soon', 0, 'refugees', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The Catholic bishops'' conference asked dioceses to raise emergency funds for communities hit by the 8 June 2026 Mindanao quake. Gifts go through diocesan social action centers and Caritas Philippines for relief and rehabilitation.

Source: https://interaksyon.philstar.com/?p=314728', '2026-06-09'),
  ('ph-cfc-build-my-church-nangalisan', 'Build the St. Joseph mission chapel in Nangalisan, Tuba', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'worship', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Couples for Christ and the Diocese of Baguio are building a chapel to serve as a mission station for about 546 families in Nangalisan, Benguet. Gifts go to CFC Global Mission Foundation''s Build My Church fund; no target amount is stated.

Source: https://couplesforchristglobal.org/come-build-our-church-in-nangalisan/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-suwalin-evangelical-fellowship', 'Church building that doubles as evacuation center ($15,000)', 'funding', 'soon', 0, 'shelter', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The fellowship needs $15,000 for a solid church building among the Mangyan near Puerto Galera that the community can also use as an evacuation center during storms.

Source: https://www.acts29.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/ChurchtoChurch-SuwalinEvangelical.pdf', '2025-10-01'),
  ('ph-suwalin-evangelical-fellowship', 'Sanitation facilities for Mangyan church site ($2,000)', 'funding', 'soon', 0, 'health', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The church has listed $2,000 for sanitation facilities at its site serving indigenous Mangyan communities in Puerto Galera.

Source: https://www.acts29.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/ChurchtoChurch-SuwalinEvangelical.pdf', '2025-10-01'),
  ('ph-suwalin-evangelical-fellowship', 'Water supply for the church and community ($2,000)', 'funding', 'soon', 0, 'water', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The church is asking for $2,000 to put in a water supply. It also asks for help securing land for future church plants among unreached Mangyan communities.

Source: https://www.acts29.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/ChurchtoChurch-SuwalinEvangelical.pdf', '2025-10-01'),
  ('ph-oms-philippines-juan-project', 'Ministry van for church-planting trainers', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'leadership', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The OMS Philippines team needs a van so pastors and church-planting leaders can travel to train others in the provinces, sometimes driving up to 15 hours a day. The van would also carry short-term mission teams. Gifts go to OMS project account #408413.

Source: https://www.onemissionsociety.org/Projects/detail/juan-project-ministry-van', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-mercy-in-action-olongapo-2', 'Free births for poor mothers ($305k still to raise)', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'health', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Mercy In Action''s GlobalGiving project has a $500,000 goal, with about $305,000 still to raise for free childbirth care. On the price list, $150 pays for one safe delivery and $500 buys a month of reusable clinic supplies.

Source: https://cl.globalgiving.org/projects/mercy-in-action-birth-center-saves-motherbaby-lives/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-mercy-in-action-olongapo-2', 'First 1,000 Days home visits for newborns ($46k remaining)', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Midwives visit mothers and babies at home after birth through the child''s first 1,000 days. The project has $46,170 left of a $98,000 goal, and $200 covers all visits for one baby.

Source: https://cl.globalgiving.org/projects/mercy-in-actions-first-1000-days/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-action-brand-new-day', 'Building fund: a home for 70+ at-risk children', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'shelter', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Brand New Day is building on its own land to house more than 70 children, up from 14 in rented space, and to give them education and skills training. Phases begin with a shelter building, then a multipurpose hall, a basketball court and more shelters as funds come in.

Source: https://www.actioninternational.org/project/Philippines-Brand-New-Day-Building-Fund', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-action-project-pagasa', 'Build a trauma-informed school building', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'education', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'On land donated in 2019, Project Pag-asa plans an accessible school building with a library, computer room and basketball court for 60+ children from orphanages. Construction may go in phases as funds are raised.

Source: https://www.actioninternational.org/project/Philippines-Project-Pag-asa-Building-Fund', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-action-project-pagasa', 'Scholarships for graduates going on to further study', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'education', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The scholarship fund pays for college or vocational study for Project Pag-asa graduates, children who have been through trauma, so that cost does not keep them from continuing.

Source: https://www.actioninternational.org/project/Philippines-Project-Pag-asa-Scholarship-Fund', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-shalom-birthing-home', 'Operating costs for maternity and newborn care', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'health', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Shalom moved to outpatient services in 2026 and needs operating funds for prenatal and postpartum care, cervical cancer screening, newborn checks, and its ''Little Warriors'' support for babies with complex medical needs.

Source: https://www.actioninternational.org/project/Philippines-Shalom-Christian-Birthing-Home-Operating-Expenses', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-working-hands-cavite', 'Sponsor vocational and discipleship training for street youth', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'work', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Gifts pay for an 8–10 month residential program for men aged 18–25 from Manila''s streets: auto mechanics, welding, woodwork or computers, daily discipleship, dorm and meals, then 1,000 hours of on-the-job training.

Source: https://www.actioninternational.org/project/Philippines-Working-Hands', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-timothy-project-lighthouse', 'Support Lighthouse shelter for abandoned and abused children', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'children', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The Lighthouse has cared for nearly 100 abandoned newborns, abused children and teens since 2017. It has built a new facility on its own property and plans more buildings, and donations fund care and expansion.

Source: https://www.actioninternational.org/project/timothy-project', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-chog-philippines-tlc', 'Wi-Fi learning hubs in rural tribal churches', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'education', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Phase 1 puts Wi-Fi antennas and routers in rural churches so children who walk 3–6 km to poor schools can join lessons streamed from Manila Church of God schools. Community Wi-Fi income then helps pay pastors and church-planting transport. No total cost is stated.

Source: https://chogglobal.org/mission-projects/projects-asia-pacific/philippinestlc/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-ethnos360-tagbanwa', 'Tagbanwa Church Planting Project', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'discipleship', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The project supports ministry among Palawan''s Southern Tagbanwa: 19 village churches, worship and leader training, medical and dental help, and translation. Gifts go through Ethnos360 with the project noted in the memo, and the latest appeal was posted in September 2026.

Source: https://blogs.ethnos360.org/jody-crain/', '2026-09-21'),
  ('ph-imb-mission-force-southern-ph', '2026 budget: wells, transport, training for tribal outreach ($55,750)', 'funding', 'soon', 0, 'discipleship', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'The team''s 2026 goal is $55,750, with only $3,100 raised when the page was updated. The money covers water wells, fuel and transport, training national believers, women''s prayer networks, discipleship, missionary care and digital outreach among unreached groups in the southern Philippines.

Source: https://www.imb.org/give/project/rescue-the-perishing-human-needs-ministry/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-phog-borongan', 'Raise the Roof: materials for Charity Village community center', 'supplies', 'soon', 0, 'shelter', true, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'Donations buy building materials for a community center in Borongan that will mainly be a typhoon refuge for the poorest villagers. It will also host education, skills training and children''s camps run with the Oikos Sisters.

Source: https://www.givegab.com/nonprofits/the-poor-household-of-god/campaigns/phog-raise-the-roof', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-gho-cmda-leyte', 'Physicians, NPs and PAs for Leyte clinic team (Mar 2027)', 'volunteers', 'soon', 0, 'health', false, '16 days on site (Mar 10-25, 2027)', array['Physician', 'Nurse practitioner', 'Physician assistant']::text[], 'Global Health Outreach is recruiting medical providers for about seven days of clinics around Matalom, Leyte, including at least one day on a small offshore island of 4,400 people with almost no local healthcare. Cost is $2,395 plus airfare and a $150 application fee.

Source: https://gho.servicereef.com/events/global-health-outreach-2/b448ffea-9be3-4c95-9925-9fdc4cb7d1ee', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-gho-cmda-leyte', 'Dentists and dental hygienists for Leyte mission (Mar 2027)', 'volunteers', 'soon', 0, 'health', false, '16 days on site (Mar 10-25, 2027)', array['Dentistry', 'Dental hygiene']::text[], 'The March 2027 Leyte team lists dentists and dental hygienists among the roles it needs for its clinics in an underserved part of the island. Participants pay $2,395 plus airfare.

Source: https://gho.servicereef.com/events/global-health-outreach-2/b448ffea-9be3-4c95-9925-9fdc4cb7d1ee', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-gho-cmda-leyte', 'Ophthalmologists and dermatologists for Leyte team', 'volunteers', 'soon', 0, 'health', false, '16 days on site (Mar 10-25, 2027)', array['Ophthalmology', 'Dermatology']::text[], 'Global Health Outreach specifically asks for eye and skin specialists to join its 2027 Leyte clinics, where most patients have little or no access to care.

Source: https://gho.servicereef.com/events/global-health-outreach-2/b448ffea-9be3-4c95-9925-9fdc4cb7d1ee', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-gho-cmda-leyte', 'Nurses, pharmacists, EMTs and non-medical servants for Leyte', 'volunteers', 'soon', 0, 'health', false, '16 days on site (Mar 10-25, 2027)', array['Nursing', 'Pharmacy', 'EMT/Paramedic']::text[], 'The team also needs nurses, pharmacists, EMTs and paramedics, first responders and non-medical helpers to run its clinics in Matalom and a nearby island. Trip leader contact is through the posting.

Source: https://gho.servicereef.com/events/global-health-outreach-2/b448ffea-9be3-4c95-9925-9fdc4cb7d1ee', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-adventist-medical-center-manila', 'Physicians and APPs for Manila primary care trip (Nov 5-15)', 'volunteers', 'urgent', 0, 'health', false, '11 days on site (Nov 5-15, 2026)', array['Physician', 'Advanced practice provider', 'Primary care']::text[], 'AdventHealth Global Missions and Adventist Medical Center Manila run free primary-care clinics for communities near the hospital; providers give consultations. Total cost is $2,750, with the final $1,275 payment due October 9, 2026.

Source: https://adventhealth.servicereef.com/events/adventhealth-global-missions/philippines-primary-care-mission-trip-373858401', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-adventist-medical-center-manila', 'Nurses for triage at Manila free clinics (Nov 2026)', 'volunteers', 'urgent', 0, 'health', false, '11 days on site (Nov 5-15, 2026)', array['Nursing', 'Triage']::text[], 'Nursing volunteers handle triage and nursing care at the November 2026 free primary-care clinics run with Adventist Medical Center Manila.

Source: https://adventhealth.servicereef.com/events/adventhealth-global-missions/philippines-primary-care-mission-trip-373858401', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-adventist-medical-center-manila', 'Pharmacy, PT/OT, imaging and lab volunteers (Nov 2026)', 'volunteers', 'urgent', 0, 'health', false, '11 days on site (Nov 5-15, 2026)', array['Pharmacy', 'Physical therapy', 'Laboratory', 'Imaging']::text[], 'Allied clinical volunteers such as pharmacists, physical and occupational therapists, imaging and lab staff are wanted to support care at the Manila primary-care clinics.

Source: https://adventhealth.servicereef.com/events/adventhealth-global-missions/philippines-primary-care-mission-trip-373858401', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-adventist-medical-center-manila', 'Non-clinical helpers for clinic operations (Nov 2026)', 'volunteers', 'urgent', 0, 'health', false, '11 days on site (Nov 5-15, 2026)', array['Registration', 'Logistics']::text[], 'The AdventHealth trip also takes non-clinical volunteers to keep clinic operations running for the free community care days near Adventist Medical Center Manila.

Source: https://adventhealth.servicereef.com/events/adventhealth-global-missions/philippines-primary-care-mission-trip-373858401', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-adventist-medical-center-bacolod', 'Partners for Negros Island''s first cardiac cath lab', 'partners', 'ongoing', 0, 'health', false, null, array['Cardiology', 'Healthcare philanthropy']::text[], 'AdventHealth Global Missions lists a cardiac catheterization lab being developed at Adventist Medical Center Bacolod as a current project; it would be the first on Negros Island.

Source: https://www.adventhealth.com/global-missions/philippines', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-hhmm-tanauan-batangas', 'General surgeons and anesthesiologists for Batangas mission', 'volunteers', 'soon', 0, 'health', false, '9 days on site (Feb 19-27, 2027)', array['General surgery', 'Anesthesiology']::text[], 'The February 2027 Tanauan/Talisay mission is a surgical mission; common cases include hernias and thyroid goiters. Cost is $950 plus a $50 application fee, applications close January 1, 2027, and 34 of 40 spots were open.

Source: https://hhmm.servicereef.com/events/helping-hands-medical-missions/philippines-tanauan-batangas-2027-mission', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-hhmm-tanauan-batangas', 'Family medicine providers for Batangas clinics (Feb 2027)', 'volunteers', 'soon', 0, 'health', false, '9 days on site (Feb 19-27, 2027)', array['Family medicine', 'Primary care']::text[], 'Family medicine providers are needed to treat the hypertension, diabetes, respiratory, gastric and skin conditions common around Tanauan, Batangas.

Source: https://hhmm.servicereef.com/events/helping-hands-medical-missions/philippines-tanauan-batangas-2027-mission', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-hhmm-tanauan-batangas', 'Dentists and optometrists for Batangas mission (Feb 2027)', 'volunteers', 'soon', 0, 'health', false, '9 days on site (Feb 19-27, 2027)', array['Dentistry', 'Optometry']::text[], 'Helping Hands Medical Missions lists dentists and optometrists among the specialties needed; dental infections are a major local issue and more than 5,500 people have received dental care on past trips.

Source: https://hhmm.servicereef.com/events/helping-hands-medical-missions/philippines-tanauan-batangas-2027-mission', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-hhmm-tanauan-batangas', 'Nurses and OR personnel for surgical mission (Feb 2027)', 'volunteers', 'soon', 0, 'health', false, '9 days on site (Feb 19-27, 2027)', array['Nursing', 'Operating room']::text[], 'Nurses and operating-room staff are needed to support surgeries and clinics during the 2027 Batangas mission.

Source: https://hhmm.servicereef.com/events/helping-hands-medical-missions/philippines-tanauan-batangas-2027-mission', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-hhmm-tanauan-batangas', 'Pharmacists and physical therapists for Batangas mission', 'volunteers', 'soon', 0, 'health', false, '9 days on site (Feb 19-27, 2027)', array['Pharmacy', 'Physical therapy']::text[], 'The posting also lists pharmacists and physical therapists among the roles needed for the February 2027 mission.

Source: https://hhmm.servicereef.com/events/helping-hands-medical-missions/philippines-tanauan-batangas-2027-mission', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-hhmm-tanauan-batangas', 'Non-medical volunteers for Batangas mission (Feb 2027)', 'volunteers', 'soon', 0, 'health', false, '9 days on site (Feb 19-27, 2027)', '{}', 'Non-medical volunteers are welcome to help run the clinics and share the Gospel during the Tanauan/Talisay mission.

Source: https://hhmm.servicereef.com/events/helping-hands-medical-missions/philippines-tanauan-batangas-2027-mission', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-palawan-baptist-hospital', 'Long-term medical missionaries for Palawan Baptist Hospital', 'expertise', 'ongoing', 0, 'health', false, 'Long-term', array['Physician', 'Nursing']::text[], 'The hospital says it needs well-trained medical missionaries so the ministry can grow; physicians, nurses and other medical professionals are invited to serve.

Source: https://abwe.org/palawan-baptist-hospital/', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-palawan-baptist-hospital', 'Ambulance, newborn equipment and a new hospital building', 'funding', 'ongoing', 0, 'health', false, 'one-off gift', '{}', 'ABWE''s giving page asks for an infant warmer and bili-light, an ambulance to move patients to higher-level care, and a new building to replace the 1979 structure, which is considered a fire hazard. Suggested gifts start at $30.

Source: https://give.abwe.org/projects/palawan-baptist-hospital', '2026-10-06'),
  ('ph-mercy-in-action-olongapo-2', 'Midwifery and maternal-health learners at birth center', 'volunteers', 'ongoing', 0, 'health', false, null, array['Midwifery', 'Nursing', 'Public health']::text[], 'Through INMED, the Olongapo birth center takes midwives, nurse-midwives, nurses, physicians, public health professionals and students interested in maternal and child health. Places are limited, and learners are asked to contact INMED about availability.

